==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Endless}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|endeles}}, from {{inh|en|ang|endelēas||endless}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*andijalausaz||endless}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|end|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛndlɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{hyph|lang=en|end|less}}
* {{audio|En-us-endless.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Having no [[end]].
#: '''''endless''' time; '''endless''' praise''
# Extending [[indefinite]]ly.
#: ''an '''endless''' line''
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Without profitable end; fruitless; unsatisfying.
#* Beaumont and Fletcher
#*: All loves are '''endless'''.

